    "text": "<p>Find the <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> coordinate of the centre of mass of the non-uniform rod of length <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> given below. The origin is taken at the left end of the rod. The density of the rod as a function of its <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>-coordinate is <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ax</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>bx</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>,&nbsp;where <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mstyle></math> and <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math> are constants.</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-06-20_at_8.48.12_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 76px;\" /></p>\r\r<p>&nbsp;</p>\r",
